By "in character", I was referring to actions taken by the hero in the
game world, while "out of character" would be something that the
player does without involving the hero directly. In NetHack, for
example, stat development happens entirely in character, while skill
development happens both in character (i.e. training) and out of
character (i.e. skill advancement via the #enhance screen).

